.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-list - List the recordings you may see


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List recordings you may replay, one per line: ID, machine, start time, length (or
"recording" while it runs), trigger and state. Team admins see all of a team's recordings;
other members see the ones they may replay. --team defaults to the active workspace (in
Personal, your own); --machine limits the list to one machine ID. The list stops at --limit
unless you pass --all.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	show every item, up to 10000

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	show at most this many items (1-200)

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	only this machine's recordings (machine id)

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team whose recordings to list; defaults to the active workspace (personal: your own)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recordings list
  pb recordings list --team acme --machine m_abc123
  pb recordings list --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings(1)\fP
